Hi guys,

I'm pasting a note from a former Deputy Ag Commissioner for SLO County who has been on our Cuesta Ag Advisory Board for years. This was a note in response to my inquiry about drone expertise in ag or contacts that could help with that:

Hi Amy,
In addition to standard drone regulations, a separate license is required to apply pesticides. Contact CeRae Spaidel at the County Agricultural Department for guidance. She oversees the county's pesticide program and can be reached at 805-781-5910<tel:805-781-5910>.
Drone operators applying pesticides must understand and comply with California pesticide laws and regulations. This knowledge should be a core component of their operational program.
Have a wonderful rest of the week
Edwin



Amy Stapp
Division Chair, Agriculture
Agriculture Business and Business Faculty
Cuesta College
805-704-4728


